{
  "question_id": "q_083_long_calls_growth",
  "slug": "long-calls-growth",
  "title": "Patient Support Analysis (Part 4)",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "company": "UnitedHealth",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "UnitedHealth customer operations monitors call center volume growth over time.\n\nA call is a **long call** if `call_duration_secs` is greater than 300 (5 minutes).\n\nFor every calendar month that has at least one call of any kind in `callers`, count the long calls and compute the month-over-month growth versus the previous month in the data:\n• `growth_pct = 100 * (current - previous) / previous`, rounded to 1 decimal place.\n• It is `NULL` for the first month, and whenever the previous month had zero long calls.\n\nOutput `call_month` (formatted `'YYYY-MM'`), `long_call_count` and `growth_pct`, ordered by `call_month`.",
  "notes": [
    "Months that have calls but no long calls count as 0 long calls.",
    "Growth is NULL for the first month, and whenever the previous month had 0 long calls (division by zero)."
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "callers",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "policy_holder_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "case_id",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "call_category",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "call_date",
          "data_type": "DATETIME"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "call_duration_secs",
          "data_type": "INT"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
